{"description":"GitHub issue maleolabs/eka-cli#25 (suggestion, low, source: agent, EKA 1.2.0): authoring an 18-object planning package cost 36 sequential MCP round trips; reporter claims no batch surface and no MCP draft mutation, forcing hand-editing of workspace files.\n\nRevision 2 (2026-08-26, planning-time amendment): tool inventory refreshed against the deployed surface (~20 tools now: get, domain, status, context, validate, new, publish, transition, note, view [deprecated alias of draft_read], draft_list, draft_read, integrity_check, discard, assign/reassign/unassign, feedback_new/feedback_publish/feedback_list, sync_push). The v1 inventory (13 tools) is superseded by this list. The TWO CORE GAPS STAND, re-verified live on 2026-08-26:\n- STILL no tool mutates an existing draft after scaffolding - no draft_update/edit exists on the boundary; eka edit remains TTY-only.\n- publish STILL accepts exactly one target per call (observed first-hand: four objects published sequentially this session); batch modes exist at CLI level but are not exposed on the MCP boundary.\n\nDesign inconsistency RE-VERIFIED against the deployed binary itself: its embedded skills documentation still instructs agents to 'edit the draft file directly' at known filesystem paths (2 occurrences in the installed binary), contradicting the 'never touch workspace storage by hand' boundary - while the new report deliberately NEVER reveals the draft path, so an MCP-only agent is told to bypass a boundary it cannot even locate.\n\nStill-valid facts from source review: batch publishing EXISTS at CLI level (eka publish --all/--pending, topological order, cmd/authoring_batch.go) and eka new --file \u003cbatch.json\u003e scaffolds a related draft set in one call.\n\nFix direction (unchanged): (1) MCP draft_update tool (target + partial content merge) to close the sanctioned-boundary hole - highest value; (2) expose batch mode on MCP publish at parity with CLI; (3) DECLINE scaffold+publish single-call merging - it conflates two lifecycle steps and weakens the draft gate.","acceptanceCriteria":"- New MCP tool draft_update (target + partial content merge) mutates a pending draft strictly inside the sanctioned API surface, pairing with the existing draft_read for read-modify-write; publish still validates the final artifact (mutation does not bypass CKO gates).\n- MCP publish tool exposes batch mode (--pending/--all parity with CLI topological batch publish).\n- Skills/docs surfaces that instruct direct draft-file editing (verified still embedded in the deployed build as of 2026-08-26) are updated to reference draft_update instead.\n- Reporter's option 3 (merge scaffold+publish into one call) formally declined with rationale recorded in the closing comment: it collapses two lifecycle steps and weakens the draft review gate that immutable/gated authoring depends on.\n- Tests cover draft_update merge semantics (partial overwrite, unknown target refusal, post-publish refusal) and batch publish ordering.\n- Review findings posted as a comment on maleolabs/eka-cli#25; issue closed only after the fix ships in a release."}